<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mrs. Tubman is a 75-year-old woman with chronic post-traumatic headache on candesartan 16 mg for prevention and provisional narcolepsy without cataplexy on modafinil 100 mg each morning, who asked for a same-day visit. Two days ago, a day after a community supper at which several other guests later became ill, she developed sudden nausea and vomited four times, followed by watery diarrhea six to eight times a day. The vomiting stopped yesterday; the diarrhea is easing, with three loose stools since midnight. There has been no blood or black stool. Her highest temperature at home was 37.8 °C. She has kept down small sips of water and broth since yesterday afternoon but little food. Her urine has been dark and less frequent, and she has felt light-headed when she stands up, without fainting or falling. She took candesartan and modafinil yesterday and this morning. A dull headache came with the illness; she took acetaminophen on both days and no ibuprofen, keeping to her headache plan. She has had two unplanned sleep episodes in the past two days, both while seated, compared with her recent rare episodes. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Two days ago, a day after a community supper</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Diffuse abdominal cramping</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>Two days; vomiting stopped yesterday</td></tr><tr><td>Character</td><td>Watery, non-bloody diarrhea; cramping before stools</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Moderate; six to eight stools a day at worst, three since midnight</td></tr><tr><td>Timing</td><td>Improving</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Other guests at the same supper became ill</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Small sips of water and broth tolerated since yesterday</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>Dark, scant urine; light-headed on standing; dull headache; two unplanned sleep episodes while seated. Denies blood in stool, fainting, falls, and fever above 37.8 °C</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

