    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Acute viral gastroenteritis, likely norovirus, with mild dehydration (A08.4)</content>. Acute watery, non-bloody diarrhea after a common-source exposure, already improving, with low-grade temperature only. Mild volume depletion: orthostatic change, dry mouth, and a creatinine of 1.21 mg/dL (eGFR 47), up from 0.88 in August, a prerenal rise while taking an angiotensin receptor blocker. Stool testing and antibiotics are not indicated for uncomplicated watery diarrhea of less than a week. [S]<list><item>Oral rehydration solution in small, frequent amounts, aiming for pale urine; then a normal diet as tolerated.</item><item>Loperamide may be used for comfort if there is no fever above 38 °C and no blood in the stool.</item><item>Hand washing with soap and water, which works better than alcohol gel against norovirus; clean bathroom surfaces with a bleach solution; do not prepare food for others until 48 hours after symptoms end.</item><item>Rise slowly, sit to wash, and have someone nearby when she showers until the light-headedness is gone.</item><item>Return or call the same day for blood in the stool, temperature above 38.5 °C, no urine for 12 hours, inability to keep fluids down, fainting, or a fall.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Chronic post-traumatic headache on candesartan (G44.329)</content>. Headache with dehydration on two days, managed within her limit of acute medicine on no more than 2 days a week. Candesartan with volume depletion raises the risk of kidney injury. [S]<list><item>Hold candesartan until she has been eating and drinking normally for a full day, then restart 16 mg daily.</item><item>Acetaminophen as needed, no more than 3 g a day and within her 2-days-a-week limit; no ibuprofen or other NSAIDs, which can harm the kidneys during dehydration and risk a return of medication-overuse headache.</item><item>Repeat the basic metabolic panel one to two weeks after restarting candesartan, at the wellness visit.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Provisional narcolepsy without cataplexy on modafinil (G47.429)</content>. More unplanned sleep episodes during an acute illness, as expected with poor sleep and dehydration. [S]<list><item>Continue modafinil 100 mg each morning once she is keeping fluids down.</item><item>Keep the two scheduled naps and add rest as needed; sit down for tasks while she is unwell.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Treatment of central disorders of hypersomnolence: an American Academy of Sleep Medicine clinical practice guideline (Maski K, et al. J Clin Sleep Med 2021;17(9):1881-1893) (2021); The International Classification of Headache Disorders, 3rd edition (Cephalalgia 2018;38(1):1-211) (2018); 2017 Infectious Diseases Society of America Clinical Practice Guidelines for the Diagnosis and Management of Infectious Diarrhea (Shane AL, et al. Clin Infect Dis 2017;65(12):e45-e80) (2017)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Nurse telephone check in two days. Wellness visit in about two weeks, with a repeat basic metabolic panel. Next scheduled visit 1897-10-13: subsequent annual wellness visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

